\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium text-[13.5px] text-white tracking-[-0.005em]\",\"children\":[\"Visual / interactive debugging\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 block font-mono font-normal text-[10.5px] text-white/50 tracking-[0.04em]\",\"children\":\"Side-by-side diffs, live preview, hover-driven inspection\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"max-sm:col-span-1 sm:col-span-1\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative h-2.5 overflow-hidden rounded-[3px] bg-white/10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute inset-0 rounded-[3px] bg-[linear-gradient(90deg,var(--color-ignition),var(--color-ignition-2))]\",\"style\":{\"width\":\"78%\"}}],false]}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-right font-medium font-mono text-[14px] text-white tracking-[-0.01em] sm:text-right\",\"children\":\"Cursor 3\"}],\"$L9a\"]}],\"$L9b\",\"$L9c\",\"$L9d\"]}],\"$L9e\"]}]\n9f:T6e7,max-w-[720px] [\u0026_*:where(p,h3,ul)]:text-pretty [\u0026_a.link:hover]:bg-ignition/10 [\u0026_a.link:hover]:text-ignition [\u0026_a.link]:border-ignition [\u0026_a.link]:border-b [\u0026_a.link]:pb-px [\u0026_a.link]:font-medium [\u0026_a.link]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_a.link]:transition-colors [\u0026_a.link]:dark:text-white [\u0026_code]:rounded-[4px] [\u0026_code]:bg-zinc-100 [\u0026_code]:px-1.5 [\u0026_code]:py-0.5 [\u0026_code]:font-mono [\u0026_code]:text-[0.88em] [\u0026_code]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_code]:dark:bg-zinc-800 [\u0026_code]:dark:text-white [\u0026_h3]:mt-9 [\u0026_h3]:mb-3.5 [\u0026_h3]:font-medium [\u0026_h3]:text-[22px] [\u0026_h3]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_h3]:leading-tight [\u0026_h3]:tracking-[-0.015em] [\u0026_h3]:dark:text-white [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:mb-2.5 [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:pl-[6px] [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:text-[16px] [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:text-zinc-700 [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:leading-[1.6] [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:marker:font-medium [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:marker:text-ignition [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:marker:tabular-nums [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:dark:text-zinc-300 [\u0026_ol:not([class])]:mb-6 [\u0026_ol:not([class])]:list-decimal [\u0026_ol:not([class])]:pl-[22px] [\u0026_p.lede]:mb-7 [\u0026_p.lede]:font-normal [\u0026_p.lede]:text-[19px] [\u0026_p.lede]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_p.lede]:leading-[1.6] [\u0026_p.lede]:dark:text-white [\u0026_p]:mb-5 [\u0026_p]:text-[17px] [\u0026_p]:text-zinc-800 [\u0026_p]:leading-[1.7] [\u0026_p]:dark:text-zinc-200 [\u0026_strong]:font-semibold [\u0026_strong]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_strong]:dark:text-white [\u0026_ul]:mb-6 [\u0026_ul]:ml-0 [\u0026_ul]:list-none [\u0026_ul]:p-0 [\u0026_ul_li]:relative [\u0026_ul_li]:mb-2.5 [\u0026_ul_li]:pl-[22px] [\u0026_ul_li]:text-[16px] [\u0026_ul_li]:text-zinc-700 [\u0026_ul_li]:leading-[1.6] [\u0026_ul_li]:before:absolute [\u0026_ul_li]:before:top-[11px] [\u0026_ul_li]:before:left-0.5 [\u0026_ul_li]:before:size-1.5 [\u0026_ul_li]:before:rounded-full [\u0026_ul_li]:before:bg-ignition [\u0026_ul_li]:before:content-[''] [\u0026_ul_li]:dark:text-zinc-30064:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"$9f\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"The pattern is consistent: Cursor 3 wins where the editor surface is part of the work — visual design, multi-agent orchestration in one UI, side-by-side rendering and diffing. Claude Code wins where the terminal is the primary surface — long-running headless sessions, deep filesystem orchestration, hooks and skills, CI integration. Neither of those is a value judgment; they're different design centers for different kinds of work. For a deeper look at the Claude Code side of that comparison, our\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L3e\",null,{\"className\":\"link\",\"href\":\"/blog/claude-code-1-3-deep-dive-features-shortcuts-config-2026\",\"children\":\"Claude Code 1.3 deep dive\"}],\" \",\"covers the configuration model, hook system, skills, and team rollout patterns.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"For teams that want the broader landscape — Cursor 3, Claude Code, Codex CLI, Windsurf, Replit and the rest — we maintain a working comparison in our\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L3e\",null,{\"className\":\"link\",\"href\":\"/blog/ai-coding-agents-claude-code-cursor-codex-replit-2026\",\"children\":\"AI coding agents review\"}],\". The short version: the right answer for most teams is two tools, not one. Cursor 3 for editor-centric work, Claude Code for terminal-centric work, with shared MCP servers and a shared model routing policy across both. If you're weighing a third editor-centric option, our\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L3e\",null,{\"className\":\"link\",\"href\":\"/blog/windsurf-2-deep-dive-cascade-agents-flows-2026\",\"children\":\"hands-on look at Windsurf 2\"}],\" \",\"walks through how its Cascade agents and Workflows compare to Cursor's surfaces.\"]}]]}]\n65:[\"$\",\"blockquote\",null,{\"className\":\"my-7 border-ignition border-l-[3px] bg-zinc-50 px-6 py-5 font-serif text-[19px] text-zinc-950 italic leading-normal tracking-[-0.005em] dark:bg-zinc-900 dark:text-white\",\"children\":[\"\\\"Cursor 3 and Claude Code aren't competitors. They're two surfaces on the same underlying work — pick by workload, run both, share the MCP servers and the routing policy across them.\\\"\",[\"$\",\"cite\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 block font-medium font-mono text-[11px] text-zinc-500 uppercase not-italic tracking-widest\",\"children\":\"— Digital Applied review, May 2026\"}]]}]\n66:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 mt-14 mb-5 scroll-mt-[90px] font-normal text-[clamp(26px,3vw,36px)] text-zinc-950 leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.025em] dark:text-white\",\"id\":\"rollout-pitfalls\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3.5 block font-medium font-mono text-[11px] text-ignition uppercase tracking-[0.12em]\",\"children\":[\"07\",\" — \",\"Pitfalls\"]}],[\"Four ways the rollout\",\" \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"className\":\"font-normal font-serif text-ignition-2 italic\",\"children\":\"trips\"}],\".\"]]}]\na0:T6e7,max-w-[720px] [\u0026_*:where(p,h3,ul)]:text-pretty [\u0026_a.link:hover]:bg-ignition/10 [\u0026_a.link:hover]:text-ignition [\u0026_a.link]:border-ignition [\u0026_a.link]:border-b [\u0026_a.link]:pb-px [\u0026_a.link]:font-medium [\u0026_a.link]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_a.link]:transition-colors [\u0026_a.link]:dark:text-white [\u0026_code]:rounded-[4px] [\u0026_code]:bg-zinc-100 [\u0026_code]:px-1.5 [\u0026_code]:py-0.5 [\u0026_code]:font-mono [\u0026_code]:text-[0.88em] [\u0026_code]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_code]:dark:bg-zinc-800 [\u0026_code]:dark:text-white [\u0026_h3]:mt-9 [\u0026_h3]:mb-3.5 [\u0026_h3]:font-medium [\u0026_h3]:text-[22px] [\u0026_h3]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_h3]:leading-tight [\u0026_h3]:tracking-[-0.015em] [\u0026_h3]:dark:text-white [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:mb-2.5 [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:pl-[6px] [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:text-[16px] [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:text-zinc-700 [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:leading-[1.6] [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:marker:font-medium [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:marker:text-ignition [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:marker:tabular-nums [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:dark:text-zinc-300 [\u0026_ol:not([class])]:mb-6 [\u0026_ol:not([class])]:list-decimal [\u0026_ol:not([class])]:pl-[22px] [\u0026_p.lede]:mb-7 [\u0026_p.lede]:font-normal [\u0026_p.lede]:text-[19px] [\u0026_p.lede]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_p.lede]:leading-[1.6] [\u0026_p.lede]:dark:text-white [\u0026_p]:mb-5 [\u0026_p]:text-[17px] [\u0026_p]:text-zinc-800 [\u0026_p]:leading-[1.7] [\u0026_p]:dark:text-zinc-200 [\u0026_strong]:font-semibold [\u0026_strong]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_strong]:dark:text-white [\u0026_ul]:mb-6 [\u0026_ul]:ml-0 [\u0026_ul]:list-none [\u0026_ul]:p-0 [\u0026_ul_li]:relative [\u0026_ul_li]:mb-2.5 [\u0026_ul_li]:pl-[22px] [\u0026_ul_li]:text-[16px] [\u0026_ul_li]:text-zinc-700 [\u0026_ul_li]:leading-[1.6] [\u0026_ul_li]:before:absolute [\u0026_ul_li]:before:top-[11px] [\u0026_ul_li]:before:left-0.5 [\u0026_ul_li]:before:size-1.5 [\u0026_ul_li]:before:rounded-full [\u0026_ul_li]:before:bg-ignition [\u0026_ul_li]:before:content-[''] [\u0026_ul_li]:dark:text-zinc-30067:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"$a0\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"We've watched four predictable failure modes in the first two weeks of team rollouts of Cursor 3. None of them are bugs; they're the natural friction of introducing multi-agent workflows into a team that previously used single-assistant tooling. Each one has a simple mitigation, but the mitigations need to be in place before the rollout, not after.\"}]}]\n68:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"my-8 flex flex-col gap-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"relative flex flex-col gap-5 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl p-6 md:flex-row md:gap-8 md:p-7 border border-zinc-200 bg-white dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-900\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-3 md:w-[220px] md:shrink-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[10.5px] text-ignition uppercase tracking-[0.14em]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"size-1.5 rounded-full bg-current shadow-[0_0_6px_currentColor]\"}],\"Pitfall 01\"]}],[\"$\",\"h5\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 font-medium text-[22px] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-zinc-950 dark:text-white\",\"children\":[\"Spawning\",\" \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"className\":\"font-normal font-serif text-ignition-2 italic\",\"children\":\"too many\"}],\" \",\"agents\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"hidden w-px self-stretch bg-zinc-200/60 md:block dark:bg-zinc-800/60\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-1 flex-col justify-between gap-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 text-[14px] leading-[1.6] text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400\",\"children\":\"Teams discover the Agents panel and immediately try to run five agents in parallel. Token burn spikes, context gets confused between agents, the human can't keep up with the approval queue. Mitigation: a working rule of no more than two writing agents at once, read-only agents on cheaper models.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"self-start pt-1 md:self-end\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-block rounded-md px-3 py-1.5 font-medium font-mono text-[11.5px] tracking-[-0.01em] bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-950 dark:bg-zinc-800 dark:text-white\",\"children\":\"Cap writing agents at 2\"}]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"relative flex flex-col gap-5 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl p-6 md:flex-row md:gap-8 md:p-7 border border-zinc-200 bg-white dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-900\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-3 md:w-[220px] md:shrink-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[10.5px] text-ignition uppercase tracking-[0.14em]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"size-1.5 rounded-full bg-current shadow-[0_0_6px_currentColor]\"}],\"Pitfall 02\"]}],[\"$\",\"h5\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 font-medium text-[22px] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-zinc-950 dark:text-white\",\"children\":\"Treating design-driven Composer as a page generator\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"hidden w-px self-stretch bg-zinc-200/60 md:block dark:bg-zinc-800/60\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-1 flex-col justify-between gap-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 text-[14px] leading-[1.6] text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400\",\"children\":\"Composer's design-driven workflow is for component scaffolding, not full-page production output. Teams that point it at a full page get UI that ships looking AI-generated — token-inconsistent, semantically thin, missing animation polish. Mitigation: scope it to one component at a time, with a designer-developer review pass.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"self-start pt-1 md:self-end\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-block rounded-md px-3 py-1.5 font-medium font-mono text-[11.5px] tracking-[-0.01em] bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-950 dark:bg-zinc-800 dark:text-white\",\"children\":\"One component at a time\"}]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"relative flex flex-col gap-5 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl p-6 md:flex-row md:gap-8 md:p-7 border border-white/10 bg-[#0a0a0b] text-white\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"style\":{\"position\":\"absolute\",\"inset\":-1,\"borderRadius\":\"16px\",\"padding\":1,\"background\":\"linear-gradient(135deg,#ff6b1a,transparent 60%)\",\"WebkitMask\":\"linear-gradient(#fff 0 0) content-box, linear-gradient(#fff 0 0)\",\"WebkitMaskComposite\":\"xor\",\"mask\":\"linear-gradient(#fff 0 0) content-box, linear-gradient(#fff 0 0)\",\"maskComposite\":\"exclude\",\"pointerEvents\":\"none\"}}],\"$La1\",\"$La2\",\"$La3\"]}],\"$La4\"]}]\na5:T6e7,max-w-[720px] [\u0026_*:where(p,h3,ul)]:text-pretty [\u0026_a.link:hover]:bg-ignition/10 [\u0026_a.link:hover]:text-ignition [\u0026_a.link]:border-ignition [\u0026_a.link]:border-b [\u0026_a.link]:pb-px [\u0026_a.link]:font-medium [\u0026_a.link]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_a.link]:transition-colors [\u0026_a.link]:dark:text-white [\u0026_code]:rounded-[4px] [\u0026_code]:bg-zinc-100 [\u0026_code]:px-1.5 [\u0026_code]:py-0.5 [\u0026_code]:font-mono [\u0026_code]:text-[0.88em] [\u0026_code]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_code]:dark:bg-zinc-800 [\u0026_code]:dark:text-white [\u0026_h3]:mt-9 [\u0026_h3]:mb-3.5 [\u0026_h3]:font-medium [\u0026_h3]:text-[22px] [\u0026_h3]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_h3]:leading-tight [\u0026_h3]:tracking-[-0.015em] [\u0026_h3]:dark:text-white [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:mb-2.5 [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:pl-[6px] [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:text-[16px] [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:text-zinc-700 [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:leading-[1.6] [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:marker:font-medium [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:marker:text-ignition [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:marker:tabular-nums [\u0026_ol:not([class])\u003eli]:dark:text-zinc-300 [\u0026_ol:not([class])]:mb-6 [\u0026_ol:not([class])]:list-decimal [\u0026_ol:not([class])]:pl-[22px] [\u0026_p.lede]:mb-7 [\u0026_p.lede]:font-normal [\u0026_p.lede]:text-[19px] [\u0026_p.lede]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_p.lede]:leading-[1.6] [\u0026_p.lede]:dark:text-white [\u0026_p]:mb-5 [\u0026_p]:text-[17px] [\u0026_p]:text-zinc-800 [\u0026_p]:leading-[1.7] [\u0026_p]:dark:text-zinc-200 [\u0026_strong]:font-semibold [\u0026_strong]:text-zinc-950 [\u0026_strong]:dark:text-white [\u0026_ul]:mb-6 [\u0026_ul]:ml-0 [\u0026_ul]:list-none [\u0026_ul]:p-0 [\u0026_ul_li]:relative [\u0026_ul_li]:mb-2.5 [\u0026_ul_li]:pl-[22px] [\u0026_ul_li]:text-[16px] [\u0026_ul_li]:text-zinc-700 [\u0026_ul_li]:leading-[1.6] [\u0026_ul_li]:before:absolute [\u0026_ul_li]:before:top-[11px] [\u0026_ul_li]:before:left-0.5 [\u0026_ul_li]:before:size-1.5 [\u0026_ul_li]:before:rounded-full [\u0026_ul_li]:before:bg-ignition [\u0026_ul_li]:before:content-[''] [\u0026_ul_li]:dark:text-zinc-300a7:I[406000,[\"$2\",\"$3\",\"$4\",\"$5\"],\"IconMark\"]\n69:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"$a5\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"The underlying pattern across all four pitfalls is the same: a multi-agent workspace surfaces choices that a single-assistant workspace never had to make. How many agents? Which model per agent? How aggressive should the auto-write behavior be? How scoped should the design-driven Composer workflow be? Teams that treat these as workspace-level governance decisions — written down, reviewed, applied as team defaults — get a meaningfully smoother rollout than teams that let each developer figure it out individually. The same pattern shows up in our broader\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L3e\",null,{\"className\":\"link\",\"href\":\"/services/ai-transformation\",\"children\":\"AI digital transformation engagements\"}],\": the tooling is rarely the limiting factor; the operating disciplines around the tooling are.\"]}]}]\n6a:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative my-10 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-[#0a0a0b] p-8 text-white\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"pointer-events-none absolute right-[-20%] bottom-[-30%] size-[400px] [background:radial-gradient(circle,rgba(255,107,26,0.12),transparent_60%)]\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative mb-3.5 flex items-center gap-2.5 font-mono text-[10.5px] text-ignition-2 uppercase tracking-[0.14em]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"size-1.5 rounded-full bg-ignition shadow-[0_0_6px_var(--color-ignition)]\"}],\"The shape of AI IDEs, May 2026\"]}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"relative m-0 mb-4 font-medium text-[22px] text-white leading-[1.2] tracking-[-0.015em]\",\"children\":\"Cursor 3 is a multi-agent IDE — pick by workload, not by brand.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative space-y-3 text-[15.5px] text-white/80 leading-[1.65]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Cursor 3 is the first AI IDE that genuinely changes the rhythm of a coding session. The parallel Agents panel, the design-driven Composer workflow, and Composer's evolved multi-file diff aren't feature increments — they're three different interaction models bundled into one workspace, each tuned to a different kind of work. Used in combination, they make AI-assisted development feel like a workspace rather than a chat box.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"The honest comparison with Claude Code is\",\" \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"className\":\"font-serif text-ignition-2 italic\",\"children\":\"workload-specific\"}],\". Cursor 3 wins for editor-centric work — visual design, mixed-model parallel sprints, side-by-side debugging. Claude Code wins for terminal-centric work — headless sessions, deep filesystem orchestration, CI integration. Neither dominates; the right answer for most teams is both, with explicit workload routing and shared MCP servers across the two.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"The broader signal is clearer than any single feature. AI IDEs are beginning to look like real workspaces — with multiple parallel agents, distinct surfaces for distinct tasks, and explicit approval gates around the writes that matter. The next twelve months of releases will sort the teams that treat that as a governance challenge (workspace defaults, routing policies, rollout disciplines) from the teams that treat it as a procurement question. The former will compound; the latter will stall.\"}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"6b:[\"$\",\"aside\",null,{\"className\":\"hidden flex-col gap-5 self-start xl:flex [@media(min-height:800px)]:sticky [@media(min-height:800px)]:top-[84px]\",\"data-blog-rail\":true,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative rounded-[18px] bg-[#0a0a0b] p-5 text-white\",\"data-newsletter-card\":true,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3.5 block font-mono text-[10.5px] text-ignition-2 uppercase tracking-[0.12em]\",\"children\":\"AI Insights\"}],[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 mb-2.5 font-medium text-[15px] text-white leading-[1.3] tracking-[-0.01em]\",\"children\":\"Deep dives on AI marketing and development.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 mb-3.5 text-[12.5px] text-white/65 leading-normal\",\"children\":\"Agentic development, frontier AI models, and data-driven strategies. No recycled AI takes.\"}],[\"$\",\"$L73\",null,{\"source\":\"blog-rail\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-900\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3.5 block font-mono text-[10.5px] text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-[0.12em]\",\"children\":\"Release window\"}],[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 mb-2.5 font-medium text-[15px] text-zinc-950 dark:text-white\",\"children\":\"Cursor 3 · May 2026\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-1 font-mono text-[12px] text-zinc-950 dark:text-white\",\"children\":\"Agents · Design · Composer\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 text-[12px] text-zinc-500 leading-normal\",\"children\":\"AI IDE surfaces move quickly. Verify the current changelog, pricing, and model availability on cursor.com before standardizing a team rollout.\"}]]}]]}]\n6d:[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3.5 block font-mono text-[11px] text-ignition-2 uppercase tracking-[0.14em]\",\"children\":\"What we work on\"}]\n6e:[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 mb-3.5 font-medium text-[19px] text-white tracking-[-0.01em]\",\"children\":\"AI IDE engagements\"}]\n6f:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 list-none p-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2.5 border-white/10 border-b py-2.5 text-[13.5px] text-white/72 last:border-b-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[13px] text-ignition\",\"children\":\"→\"}],\"Head-to-head workload comparison\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2.5 border-white/10 border-b py-2.5 text-[13.5px] text-white/72 last:border-b-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[13px] text-ignition\",\"children\":\"→\"}],\"Cursor 3 rollout playbook with Composer + Agents\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2.5 border-white/10 border-b py-2.5 text-[13.5px] text-white/72 last:border-b-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[13px] text-ignition\",\"children\":\"→\"}],\"MCP-server integration design\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2.5 border-white/10 border-b py-2.5 text-[13.5px] text-white/72 last:border-b-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[13px] text-ignition\",\"children\":\"→\"}],\"Model-routing strategy across Claude / GPT / Gemini\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2.5 border-white/10 border-b py-2.5 text-[13.5px] text-white/72 last:border-b-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[13px] text-ignition\",\"children\":\"→\"}],\"Team training and adoption cadence\"]}]]}]\n71:[\"The questions teams ask \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"before\"}],\" the IDE switch.\"]\n74:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 flex-1 text-[14px] text-zinc-500 leading-[1.55]\",\"children\":\"Hands-on deep dive into Windsurf 2 — Cascade, Workflows, multi-file edits, memory, MCP integration, and what distinguishes it from Cursor and Claude Code.\"}]\n75:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-auto flex items-center justify-between border-zinc-200 border-t pt-3.5 font-mono text-[10.5px] text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-[0.08em] dark:border-zinc-800\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"May 10, 2026\",\" · \",9,\" min\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1 font-medium text-zinc-950 dark:text-white\",\"children\":[\"Read \",[\"$\",\"$L6c\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"icon\":\"$39:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:3:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:icon\",\"className\":\"size-3.5\"}]]}]]}]\n76:[\"$\",\"$L28\",\"continue-dev-deep-dive-open-source-ai-coding-assistant-2026\",{\"className\":\"group flex min-h-[260px] flex-col gap-3.5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 bg-white p-7 transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-zinc-400 hover:shadow-[0_20px_40px_-20px_rgba(0,0,0,0.1)] dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-950\",\"href\":\"/blog/continue-dev-deep-dive-open-source-ai-coding-assistant-2026\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"self-start rounded-sm border border-ignition/20 bg-ignition/5 px-2 py-1 font-mono text-[10.5px] text-ignition uppercase tracking-[0.12em]\",\"children\":\"